istory := (p, a) :: z.2.2.2\n          if h : z.2.2.1.val + 1 < m then\n            (z.1, answers, ⟨z.2.2.1.val + 1, h⟩, history)\n          else\n            (update z.1 q (decode q answers), (fun _ => blank), ⟨0, hm⟩, history)\n      let batch := run nextB updateB primitive (m * fuel)\n        (s, (fun _ => blank), ⟨0, hm⟩, [])\n      let direct := run next update target fuel s\n      (((batch.1.1.1, batch.1.2), batch.2 / m) = direct) ∧\n      batch.2 = m * direct.2 ∧\n      direct.2 ≤ fuel ∧\n      (∀ j : J,\n        batch.1.1.2.2.2.countP (fun pa => decide (label pa.1 = j)) =\n          (List.ofFn slot).countP (fun v => decide (v = j)) * direct.2)\n","truth_boundary":"One Level B author-derived positive finite-batch canonical compiler and its associated private concrete Appendix B.1 operational consumers only. Actual raw reversed request/reply history, source state/Option readback and actual query counts are retained. Separate own FO/gradient policies use genuine internal reply/gradient reconstruction for every full Os at3≤n≤d,κ≥4,k=d/n,m=2k,2fuel<n. Exact total/per-block costs and ordinary real L1 expectation identities; stops and none exhaustion remain explicit. No universal source Alg/Q_G representation, Haar/posterior/padded Eq13 law, guaranteed successful sampler, finite precision/noisy/TV/runtime theorem, C6/L44/either main bound, main/global-site integration, purification or Goal closure. Actual math480/native witness does not mean later metadata/public trees were Lean rebuilt."},"from_state":"EXPLORING","modes":["proof-design","compiler-diagnosis","source-review"],"schema_version":4,"to_state":"PROVED_LOCAL","worker_id":"huanjian_20261116_batched_oracle_simulation"}
